---
/**
 * AccessProblemSection.astro
 *
 * The "why" moment on the homepage. Positioned between SocialProofBar and
 * WhyLessCostSection — after trust stats, before the price explanation.
 *
 * Strategic intent:
 *   The hero and social-proof bar establish WHAT USRad offers. WhyLessCost
 *   explains HOW the price works. This section answers WHY this matters —
 *   naming the access problem before the mechanics of the solution.
 *
 *   This is the strategic reframe vs. "quality-only" competitors (Covera):
 *   quality is meaningless if the patient can't access or afford the scan.
 *
 * Design notes:
 *   - Editorial register, not a feature block. Single column, generous air.
 *   - Flat white surface (design contract §7.1, no gradients).
 *   - No gold (§8.1 reserves gold for B2B recruitment CTAs; this is patient-facing).
 *   - Uses the same eyebrow treatment as about.astro chapter labels, but in navy.
 *   - Motion is restrained: one fade-up per paragraph via AOS, ≤300ms (§15.2).
 *   - Thesis line gets a subtle left rule and deeper weight — the visual anchor.
 */
---

<section class="py-24 sm:py-32 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Editorial eyebrow -->
    <div class="text-center mb-10" data-aos="fade-up">
      <p
        class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#003087] mb-3"
      >
        The Problem We Solve
      </p>
      <div class="w-12 h-[2px] bg-[#003087]/30 mx-auto"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Headline -->
    <h2
      class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-10 leading-[1.1] text-center"
      data-aos="fade-up"
      data-aos-delay="100"
    >
      Imaging shouldn't be<br class="hidden sm:block" /> this hard to access.
    </h2>

    <!-- Body narrative -->
    <div class="space-y-7 text-lg sm:text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <p data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="150">
        A scan is never just a scan. It determines diagnoses, treatment plans,
        outcomes.
      </p>

      <p data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
        But for millions of Americans, the challenge isn't just quality &mdash;
        it's whether they get imaged at all. Delayed imaging. Unclear pricing.
        No simple way to find and book the right provider.
      </p>

      <p data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="250">
        The result isn't just inconvenience. It's missed diagnoses, delayed
        care, and worse outcomes.
      </p>

      <p
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 leading-snug pt-2"
        data-aos="fade-up"
        data-aos-delay="275"
      >
        Because healthcare doesn't improve until the patient actually gets
        imaged.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Thesis / resolution line — visually distinct, the emotional pivot -->
    <div
      class="mt-14 pl-6 border-l-2 border-[#003087]"
      data-aos="fade-up"
      data-aos-delay="350"
    >
      <p class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 leading-snug">
        USRad exists to close that gap.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-gray-500 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
        The right imaging center, at a transparent price, with a clear path to
        the appointment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
